cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or data, please cite it as below."
title: "Version Context and Control Construction in Machine Learning Detection of Malicious Package Updates Across npm and PyPI"
authors:
  - family-names: "Draz"
    given-names: "Moatasem M."
    affiliation: "Department of Information Systems, Faculty of Computers and Information, Kafrelsheikh University, Kafrelsheikh, Egypt"
abstract: >-
  Dataset-construction, feature-extraction and evaluation code for a study of
  version-context detection of malicious package updates in the npm and PyPI
  registries. The study reports three control-construction designs
  (within-package, size-matched, and unmatched clean controls) under
  package-disjoint evaluation, and quantifies the contribution of version
  context relative to size confounds.
keywords:
  - software supply chain security
  - malicious package detection
  - npm
  - PyPI
  - machine learning
  - version context
  - control construction
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.22051147
repository-code: "https://github.com/moatasem2005/Version-Context-Detection-of-Malicious-Package-Updates"
license: MIT
version: "2.1.0"
date-released: "2026-08-22"
